# Integer8 literal below the minimum

Verifies a negated int8 literal whose signed magnitude is below the 8-bit
minimum is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI
pipeline.

>>> source
const too_small: int8 = -129
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `-129` for type `int8`: number too small to fit in target type at Span { start: 24, end: 28 }

<<< exit
1
